   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The quotient of consecutive terms is \\( r = \\frac{x}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} \\), the same for every n, so the series is geometric. Its first term is the \\( n = 1 \\) term, \\( a = \\frac{3 x}{2} - \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Rational",
                  3,
                  2
               ],
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Rational",
               -3,
               2
            ]
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99067",
         "rule_named": "first term and ratio"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "It converges when \\( |r| < 1 \\), that is for \\( \\left|x - 1\\right| < 4 \\).",
         "rule_named": "convergence condition"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "There the sum is \\( \\frac{a}{1 - r} = - \\frac{6 \\left(x - 1\\right)}{x - 5} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
